    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0298" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg278"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl
                        Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    note of the 8th instant, communicating to me the fact that directions have been
                    given by her Majesty’s government to prohibit any ship-of-war of either
                    belligerent from being brought into any of her ports for the purpose of being
                    dismantled or sold. I shall transmit a copy of the same for the information of
                    my government.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship, &amp;c, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
